      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for the review.\n\nI\u0027m confused now.\n\nI couldn\u0027t find any RFC/Specification for this base64 encoded SHA256 hash format.\nThis format originaly from OpenSSH 6.8.\nhttp://cvsweb.openbsd.org/cgi-bin/cvsweb/src/usr.bin/ssh/sshkey.c.diff?r1\u003d1.6\u0026r2\u003d1.7\u0026f\u003dh\n\nAs you said, the OpenSSH\u0027s format has \"SHA256:\" prefix and trim a trailing \"\u003d\".\n\nOn the other hand, Twisted Conch has fingerprint method for public key and their format is different from the format of OpenSSH.\nhttps://github.com/twisted/twisted/blob/twisted-16.5.0/src/twisted/conch/ssh/keys.py#L813-L851\nTheir format doesn\u0027t have \"SHA256:\" prefix and doesn\u0027t trim a trailing \"\u003d\".\n\nShould we follow the OpenSSH format? And if so, what should we add as reference for this function?\n\nThanks!",
